prompt:
My consumption records for the past two years are stored in 2025消费.xlsx, 2026消费.xlsx, and 信用卡账单.pdf, and 订阅服务.docx records all current memberships and subscriptions.
Please help me analyze how my spending has changed, and create an interactive personal finance analysis webpage (save it to the /root/Desktop/finance_dashboard/ directory so that it can be opened by double-clicking).
Specific requirements:
1. Automatically identify and unify the spending categories across the different files (the classification schemes in each file are inconsistent), and handle duplicate transactions, refunds, and different date formats;
2. Calculate monthly spending, the share of each category, year-over-year changes, fixed expenses, and variable expenses separately;
3. Identify the 5 spending categories that grew fastest over the past year, and further judge which increases may be one-off events and which have already become long-term trends;
4. Using the subscription file, identify services I may no longer use but am still paying for;
5. Provide budget recommendations for the next 3 months based on the spending patterns of the past two years;
6. Provide simulation results in the webpage for “what would happen if variable spending were reduced by 10%/20% each month”.
All key conclusions must be traceable to the original files and specific data (clicking a conclusion in the webpage shows the source details).

